# agy hooks, veto, sandbox and stop signal, ADR-0040 C3/C12, parity 17-19 (stage 5 of the agy spike, 2026-11-12).
# Windows 11, agy 1.5.6, isolated root --gemini_dir=<tmp>\gd (auth from the Windows keyring)
# unless marked WSL. Model: gemini-3.8-flash-low. Paths: <home> = %USERPROFILE%.
# Hook command = <python> -I <tmp>\tools\hook.py <tag> <tmp>\hooks.log; the script appends one
# JSON line per call (event, tool, conversationId, its own cwd) and prints {} (PreToolUse:
# {"decision":"allow"}, or deny when the probe asks for it).

## H0 Registration: <repo>\.agents\hooks.json (tag ws) and <gd>\config\hooks.json (tag gl),
## every event of the bundled agy-customizations/docs/hooks.md: SessionStart, PreInvocation,
## PreToolUse (matcher *), PostToolUse (matcher *), PostInvocation, Stop.
## cli.log: hooks_manager.go:53] loaded 2 named hooks from 2 hooks.json file(s)

## H1 quoted program path (shell form as C12 rule 3 would write it), workspace .agents/hooks.json + global <gd>/config/hooks.json
$ agy --gemini_dir=<tmp>\gd --model gemini-3.8-flash-low --output-format stream-json --dangerously-skip-permissions --print-timeout 120s < p1.txt
prompt: Run the shell command `echo hook-probe` with your command tool, then reply with the single word DONE.
exit=3  wall 6.6s
--- hooks.json command (each handler; the program path in double quotes, as a shell form quotes it):
"<home>\AppData\Local\Programs\Python\Python311\python.exe" -I "<tmp>\tools\hook.py" ws "<tmp>\hooks.log"
## agy runs it with `cmd /c` and Go's argv quoting, so cmd receives \"…\": the quoted path is not found.
